<title>ROMANIA: IMF approves $430 mln credits for Romania.</title>
<headline>IMF approves $430 mln credits for Romania.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Monetary Fund has approved credits totalling $430 million for Romania after agreeing on reform targets with the country's centrist government, the IMF's Bucharest office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>An IMF statement said the 13-month standby agreement, subject to two reviews, was approved on Tuesday at an Executive Board meeting in Washington.</p>
